WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
Expect to see
something different,

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.230
something scary, something
fun, and something heartfelt.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.750
[EERIE SCREAMING]

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.660
"Werewolf by Night" is a story
where a bunch of characters

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.030
are coming together for
a very frightening time.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.370
We're going to introduce
you to Jack and Elsa,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.190
and see what dangerous
adventures they get up

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.220
to over one night trapped
with a secret cabal

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.090
of monster hunters.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.810
It's kind of the first
real full exploration into

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.957
this supernatural universe.

00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:28.290
At Disney+ we
have the opportunity

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.920
to tell stories of
different levels,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.830
and so this is our first
special presentation.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.480
It's a little bit under
an hour, because it's

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.490
given you a taste--
maybe an appetizer--

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.350
of the monster side of the MCU.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.590
We went and we filmed it
completely in black and white.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.990
And I think that's going to
be a different experience

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:43.840
for everyone.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.450
LAURA DONNELLY:
It is a throwback

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.300
to the '30s and '40s
horror movies that I loved

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.510
whenever I was growing up.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.370
It's really unique.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.370
What we want to do is create
an experience for somebody

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.940
that years from now
they can go, "You

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.550
know what scared me as a kid?

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.260
This-- when I watched this.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.580
And I never forgot it."

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.100
I hope that they maybe
might go back and explore some

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.379
of those old horror movies
as well, some of those ones

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:05.880
that I loved
whenever I was a kid.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.850
I hope that audiences get
to enjoy the fun, the scares,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.910
the excitement, but also fall
in love with these characters

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.610
of Jack and Elsa, and see
where they go on their journey,

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.800
and maybe what surprising
end they come to.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.970
If I were to have to turn into
an animal under a full moon,

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:26.560
it would be some cross between
probably an ape and a wolf,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.360
I guess.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.350
I think I'd be a bat.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.910
A bat-- they're
a little scary.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:30.900
They're also a little cute.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.830
"Werewolf by Night" is scary
vintage horror with a heart.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:39.810
A love letter to every movie
I grew up watching as a kid.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.340
"Werewolf by Night" 
is the tale

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.620
you've been waiting for it
to bring you into the monster

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.700
side of the MCU.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.320
LAURA DONNELLY: Don't
miss "Werewolf by Night"

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.820
now streaming on Disney+.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.620
[EERIE SCREAMING]

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.070
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

